.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Erich Huckel&#x27;s 1931 pi-electron theory reduces a planar conjugated ring to a small matrix eigenvalue problem: one 2p_z orbital per carbon, Coulomb integral \alpha on the diagonal, and resonance integral \beta only between bonded neighbours (~chemistrykit.quantum.systems.huckel.HuckelSystem). Filling the resulting levels two electrons at a time shows why rings with 4n+2 pi electrons (benzene, 6) form a closed shell while rings with 4n (cyclobutadiene, 4) leave two electrons unpaired in a degenerate pair. is_aromatic_by_huckel_rule checks the rule against the computed degeneracies, not only by counting electrons.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/quantum/huckel/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_huckel_aromaticity_rule_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/quantum/huckel/plot_01_huckel_aromaticity_rule`

